BCR adjustment to vendor/double-conversion/upstream/BUILD.

This is double-conversion's own BUILD file, written for a workspace whose root
is the double-conversion checkout: its sources and cctest include headers as
<double-conversion/bignum.h>. Vendored under vendor/double-conversion/upstream
inside icu those paths no longer resolve, so :cctest cannot compile and any
`bazel build @icu//...` fails on it. `includes = ["."]` on the library puts the
package directory on the include path for the library and its dependents,
which is what the upstream layout provided implicitly. The library itself is
unused by icu4c (i18n carries its own copy) and already built; only the test
target changes outcome.

--- vendor/double-conversion/upstream/BUILD
+++ vendor/double-conversion/upstream/BUILD
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
         "double-conversion/strtod.h",
         "double-conversion/utils.h",
     ],
+    includes = ["."],
     linkopts = [
         "-lm",
     ],
